Airbnb End-to-End Data Engineering Pipeline
Project Overview
The Airbnb End-to-End Data Engineering Pipeline is a modern, production-grade data processing workflow built using Snowflake, dbt (Data Build Tool), AWS, and Git.

This project ingests, transforms, and models raw Airbnb data using an industry-standard Medallion Architecture (Bronze → Silver → Gold). It showcases best practices in data warehousing, including incremental data loading, Slowly Changing Dimensions (SCD Type 2) via dbt snapshots, custom Jinja macros, automated data testing, and modular SQL development.

Architecture & Data Flow
Data flows seamlessly through a structured multi-layer pipeline:

Source Data (AWS / Raw Storage) → Snowflake Staging Layer

Bronze Layer: Raw data ingestion, initial standardization, and incremental loading (bronze_bookings, bronze_hosts, bronze_listings).

Silver Layer: Data cleaning, type conversion, null handling, validation, and business rule application (silver_bookings, silver_hosts, silver_listings).

Gold Layer: Business-ready analytical tables, including a denormalized One Big Table (obt) and structured fact models (fact) tailored for reporting and dashboard consumption.

Key Technical Features
Incremental Models: Implemented across Bronze and Silver layers to process only new records, ensuring faster execution and minimized compute costs.

Slowly Changing Dimensions (SCD Type 2): Managed via dbt Snapshots (dim_bookings, dim_hosts, dim_listings) to track historical changes over time for point-in-time reporting.

Custom Jinja Macros: Reusable code logic including custom schema routing (generate_schema_name.sql), string cleanup (trimmer.sql), dynamic calculation utilities (multiply.sql), and business tagging (tag.sql).

Data Quality & Testing: Comprehensive automated testing framework covering source validation, null checks, and business rules via dbt test.

Modular SQL Development: Clean separation of concerns using ephemeral models, sources, and version-controlled transformations.

Tech Stack
Data Warehouse: Snowflake (AIRBNB.BRONZE, AIRBNB.SILVER, AIRBNB.GOLD)

Transformation Tool: dbt Core (SQL + Jinja)

Cloud Platform: AWS

Version Control: Git & GitHub

Development Environment: VS Code

Future Enhancements
CI/CD pipeline integration using GitHub Actions.

Orchestration with Apache Airflow.

Advanced monitoring, alerting, and automated Data Quality Dashboards.

Github link: https://github.com/Krishnaprasad0705/Airbnb-data-engineering-pipeline